---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import first from "../../../results/exp001/exp001.json";
import second from "../../../results/exp002/exp002.json";
const best = second.summary.find(row => row.micro_batch_size === 16)?.speedup ?? 0;
const success = [first,second].reduce((n,e)=>n+e.runs.filter(r=>r.status==="ok").length,0);
const total = first.runs.length + second.runs.length;
---
<BaseLayout title="Overview">
  <div class="eyebrow">Research lab / Overview</div>
  <h1>Can AI agents discover training speedups that transfer?</h1>
  <p class="lead">This project tests whether an optimization agent improves neural-network training throughput on unfamiliar models and GPUs—not just on the development cases it has already seen.</p>
  <div class="grid" aria-label="Current research status">
    <section class="card"><div class="muted small">EXP-002 observed speedup</div><div class="metric">{best.toFixed(2)}×</div><span class="chip">Small-model pilot only</span></section>
    <section class="card"><div class="muted small">Successful GPU pilot runs</div><div class="metric">{success}/{total}</div><span class="chip">EXP-001 and EXP-002</span></section>
    <section class="card"><div class="muted small">Research stage</div><div class="metric" style="font-size:1.45rem">Pilots measured</div><span class="chip">Full benchmark pending</span></section>
  </div>
  <h2>Learn by testing a hypothesis</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <section class="card"><h2>1. Understand</h2><p>What does a training step do? Why do batch size, precision and hardware affect speed?</p><a href="/learn">Open the learning lab</a></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>2. Measure</h2><p>Compare two Kaggle pilot measurements using fixed training workloads and validation-loss checks.</p><a href="/experiments">Compare EXP-001 and EXP-002</a></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>3. Generalize</h2><p>Test whether changes that help on a development GPU also help on unseen configurations. The pilots do not answer that yet.</p><a href="/research">Read the research protocol</a></section>
  </div>
  <p class="muted small">Results are from small synthetic-data pilots on one Tesla T4 GPU; they are not agent optimization or held-out results.</p>
</BaseLayout>
